1
00:01:31,810 --> 00:01:37,780
Two Paths.

2
00:01:33,610 --> 00:01:37,990
Can you stop me...

3
00:01:42,320 --> 00:01:46,410
as Askeladd did back then?

4
00:01:50,180 --> 00:01:52,030
Please leave, Thorfinn.

5
00:01:53,290 --> 00:01:57,130
You're a strange man,
but it'd be a shame to kill you.

6
00:02:01,610 --> 00:02:04,680
This is how the world works.

7
00:02:05,100 --> 00:02:08,780
In the end, might makes right.

8
00:02:11,270 --> 00:02:12,870
Damn Vikings.

9
00:02:19,870 --> 00:02:24,030
My foolish son.

10
00:02:25,060 --> 00:02:28,330
You're still not yet a king.

11
00:02:29,520 --> 00:02:36,750
Why did you reveal your
true feelings to such lowly men?

12
00:02:39,430 --> 00:02:44,920
Surely you don't expect that
you will understand each other.

13
00:02:46,360 --> 00:02:50,030
They're a poor flock of sheep.

14
00:02:51,450 --> 00:02:55,180
You are an aloof shepherd.

15
00:02:55,980 --> 00:03:00,910
You raise them, cull them, and skin them.

16
00:03:01,440 --> 00:03:07,570
How could the sheep understand
the work of a shepherd?

17
00:03:08,330 --> 00:03:10,940
There is only control.

18
00:03:11,790 --> 00:03:16,080
It is what's best for the sheep.

19
00:03:17,640 --> 00:03:18,940
Canute.

20
00:03:23,190 --> 00:03:28,010
If you intended to use your
authority to force your way...

21
00:03:28,470 --> 00:03:29,850
Kill him.

22
00:03:30,370 --> 00:03:33,100
He's dangerous.

23
00:03:33,770 --> 00:03:40,890
A single sheep can lead the entire flock
astray and towards a cliff.

24
00:03:42,440 --> 00:03:43,360
I will...

25
00:03:43,360 --> 00:03:44,940
Kill him.

26
00:03:45,890 --> 00:03:48,490
Do your job as king.

27
00:03:49,490 --> 00:03:50,570
I will...

28
00:03:56,500 --> 00:03:57,550
run.

29
00:04:16,850 --> 00:04:20,450
You'll simply... run?

30
00:04:25,650 --> 00:04:26,940
That's all?

31
00:04:30,050 --> 00:04:32,150
What else can I do?

32
00:04:33,160 --> 00:04:36,280
Do you want us to kill each other here?

33
00:04:40,930 --> 00:04:48,360
The paradise you describe helps
many people while oppressing few.

34
00:04:48,970 --> 00:04:51,430
That's how it works, right?

35
00:04:53,080 --> 00:04:56,650
I don't know if that's a good or bad thing,

36
00:04:57,290 --> 00:05:00,190
and I don't have the right to
criticize your crazy ideas.

37
00:05:02,070 --> 00:05:05,110
So the only option left is to run.

38
00:05:06,560 --> 00:05:08,290
Einar, let's go.

39
00:05:07,400 --> 00:05:10,570
You're an exceptional warrior.

40
00:05:08,290 --> 00:05:09,030
What?

41
00:05:10,570 --> 00:05:12,380
There are other ways.

42
00:05:13,060 --> 00:05:14,310
Did you...

43
00:05:16,760 --> 00:05:23,480
Did you let that happen to your face
merely so you could admonish me?

44
00:05:25,300 --> 00:05:27,210
I wasted my time.

45
00:05:29,300 --> 00:05:32,330
Goodbye, Your Majesty.

46
00:06:13,850 --> 00:06:14,600
There are...

47
00:06:15,620 --> 00:06:18,310
There are many who wish to bargain with me.

48
00:06:19,110 --> 00:06:21,420
Some try to ensnare me, too.

49
00:06:22,680 --> 00:06:23,720
But...

50
00:06:25,770 --> 00:06:27,730
But you're unbelievable!

51
00:06:28,300 --> 00:06:29,930
You absolute fool!

52
00:06:31,700 --> 00:06:33,900
You don't have anything up your sleeve?

53
00:06:33,900 --> 00:06:37,590
Completely unarmed and thoroughly beaten,

54
00:06:37,590 --> 00:06:40,970
you simply came to tell me
not to seize this farm?

55
00:06:44,900 --> 00:06:47,310
Is it really that funny?

56
00:06:47,890 --> 00:06:53,180
It is. I've never participated in such
ridiculous peace talks before.

57
00:07:02,340 --> 00:07:04,140
You'll run, huh?

58
00:07:08,130 --> 00:07:09,100
Yeah.

59
00:07:14,050 --> 00:07:19,350
So the Vikings are capable of
producing someone like you.

60
00:07:20,230 --> 00:07:22,060
You're a beautiful man.

61
00:07:29,330 --> 00:07:32,730
Where will you go to escape war?

62
00:07:33,720 --> 00:07:35,800
Somewhere other than here.

63
00:07:36,550 --> 00:07:38,950
I can't tell you where.

64
00:07:41,860 --> 00:07:44,590
My territory continues to grow.

65
00:07:45,220 --> 00:07:49,530
My power may eventually reach that place.

66
00:07:51,590 --> 00:07:53,990
I'll run as far as I can.

67
00:07:54,790 --> 00:07:58,710
As long as I've got
someplace to run, I won't fight.

68
00:08:00,950 --> 00:08:08,430
I'll create a peaceful place beyond the king's
reach using methods different from yours.

69
00:08:10,570 --> 00:08:15,320
For the people who can't live in
the world you create.

70
00:08:16,500 --> 00:08:20,280
For you and for me.

71
00:08:23,590 --> 00:08:28,670
So you'll fill the hole my work cannot.

72
00:08:30,840 --> 00:08:33,230
Are you capable of that?

73
00:08:35,170 --> 00:08:39,710
My power is so much smaller than yours.

74
00:08:40,170 --> 00:08:42,680
I can't fill a very large hole.

75
00:08:43,850 --> 00:08:51,640
If you keep oppressing people,
eventually no one will be able to save you.

76
00:08:54,760 --> 00:08:59,350
You need to try harder.
Don't make more work for me.

77
00:09:04,900 --> 00:09:09,420
You've become rather eloquent.

78
00:09:11,250 --> 00:09:14,510
Who did you take after?

79
00:09:29,780 --> 00:09:35,310
Interesting. I've never participated in
such challenging peace talks before.

80
00:09:43,110 --> 00:09:46,410
What... is this?

81
00:09:48,130 --> 00:09:49,530
The ships are gone.

82
00:09:50,520 --> 00:09:53,100
Where did you go, King Canute?

83
00:09:53,100 --> 00:09:54,950
You can't be serious!

84
00:09:55,940 --> 00:10:02,030
Our battle hasn't been settled yet!

85
00:10:07,050 --> 00:10:10,430
Floki was dissatisfied.

86
00:10:11,010 --> 00:10:14,120
He said he doesn't understand why
we're withdrawing from the farm.

87
00:10:16,130 --> 00:10:18,870
As you dissatisfied as well, Wulf?

88
00:10:20,630 --> 00:10:21,610
No.

89
00:10:23,790 --> 00:10:27,580
I'm canceling our plans
to seize other farms as well.

90
00:10:28,200 --> 00:10:31,110
I wouldn't want to create
more work for Thorfinn.

91
00:10:43,540 --> 00:10:50,630
Until now, I thought you were
the only one fighting with me.

92
00:10:52,450 --> 00:10:56,780
But today, I gained new allies.

93
00:11:09,650 --> 00:11:14,690
Later, Canute ordered the disbandment
of the Danish army stationed in England

94
00:11:14,690 --> 00:11:18,440
that had been pressuring English finances.

95
00:11:21,720 --> 00:11:30,840
In the end, Canute's Danish forces
dwindled to a mere 16 ships.

96
00:11:36,310 --> 00:11:41,830
However, the English uprising people
feared would occur never happened.

97
00:11:44,180 --> 00:11:49,440
The English nobility realized the
trust Canute had placed in them

98
00:11:49,440 --> 00:11:51,630
when he relinquished his military forces,

99
00:11:52,890 --> 00:11:58,540
and the relationship between conqueror
and conquered began to change.

100
00:12:16,010 --> 00:12:17,550
I feel good.

101
00:13:39,620 --> 00:13:43,800
As long as you're alive, you can...

102
00:13:50,340 --> 00:13:53,760
Why do I have to live?

103
00:14:12,450 --> 00:14:13,820
Thorfinn...

104
00:14:15,470 --> 00:14:17,610
Are you good now?

105
00:14:17,610 --> 00:14:23,540
Yeah. I still feel a little dizzy,
but I'm fine.

106
00:14:27,590 --> 00:14:30,440
Don't do crazy stuff like that.

107
00:14:31,880 --> 00:14:32,970
Sorry.

108
00:14:45,730 --> 00:14:48,470
Are we going, Thorfinn?

109
00:14:49,690 --> 00:14:52,600
To the land beyond the sea.

110
00:14:56,580 --> 00:14:58,040
You mean Vinland.

111
00:15:00,410 --> 00:15:01,950
Vinland.

112
00:15:06,230 --> 00:15:12,860
When Arnheid drew her last breath,

113
00:15:14,040 --> 00:15:17,100
I couldn't answer her right away.

114
00:15:18,570 --> 00:15:22,360
I couldn't tell her why she had to live.

115
00:15:23,700 --> 00:15:28,600
What am I supposed to say
to a soul that's been through hell

116
00:15:30,250 --> 00:15:33,150
and yearns for the peace of death?

117
00:15:40,530 --> 00:15:43,080
I want a world where I
can tell people to live.

118
00:15:44,860 --> 00:15:51,160
One I can proudly describe to people
whose only salvation is death.

119
00:15:51,780 --> 00:15:55,740
A place more appealing than death.

120
00:15:59,300 --> 00:16:09,260
That's all we ever wanted
in this world we live in.

121
00:16:30,410 --> 00:16:33,030
I won't accept it.

122
00:16:36,650 --> 00:16:39,500
If a place like that doesn't exist...

123
00:16:43,890 --> 00:16:46,510
then I'll make one.

124
00:16:51,240 --> 00:16:52,300
Einar.

125
00:17:00,120 --> 00:17:02,840
Brother, come with me.

126
00:17:03,620 --> 00:17:06,950
We'll build a peaceful land in Vinland.

127
00:17:07,680 --> 00:17:10,680
One we can proudly tell Arnheid about.

128
00:17:12,650 --> 00:17:14,750
Let's do it, brother.

129
00:17:15,250 --> 00:17:20,090
Beyond the sea, let's create
a country without slavery or war.

130
00:17:25,830 --> 00:17:27,670
For Arnheid.

131
00:18:15,060 --> 00:18:18,700
Are you sure you're okay with this?

132
00:18:20,130 --> 00:18:24,190
It was presumptuous of me to do that.

133
00:18:26,360 --> 00:18:29,070
I've told the master and
everyone on the farm

134
00:18:29,070 --> 00:18:32,620
that the young master
convinced the king to withdraw.

135
00:18:33,270 --> 00:18:34,570
Thank you.

136
00:18:36,390 --> 00:18:41,110
You can count on me to
protect Arnheid's grave.

137
00:18:46,510 --> 00:18:49,020
Truly, thank you.

138
00:18:50,180 --> 00:18:51,320
Oh, it was...

139
00:18:52,220 --> 00:18:57,070
Thorfinn, I want to be like you.

140
00:18:57,830 --> 00:19:03,850
Strong and kind like you. A real man.

141
00:19:08,890 --> 00:19:15,590
Olmar, I heard you made
the decision to stop fighting.

142
00:19:16,670 --> 00:19:18,390
That's amazing.

143
00:19:21,000 --> 00:19:24,940
It took me fifteen years to do that.

144
00:19:28,520 --> 00:19:29,390
But...

145
00:19:34,270 --> 00:19:38,730
I've finally figured out what I should do.

146
00:19:40,630 --> 00:19:43,710
This is a wonderful farm.

147
00:19:44,710 --> 00:19:47,750
I hope you'll rebuild and protect it.

148
00:19:51,460 --> 00:19:52,700
Old Master,

149
00:19:53,960 --> 00:19:59,340
thank you for always helping us.

150
00:20:01,560 --> 00:20:05,770
I told you, it was just a deal we made.

151
00:20:06,300 --> 00:20:09,130
You shouldn't be thanking me.

152
00:20:16,050 --> 00:20:20,330
I wish he would've taken
at least a single silver mark.

153
00:20:29,280 --> 00:20:32,270
Thorfinn, Einar!

154
00:20:33,850 --> 00:20:39,270
My name is Roald, Son of Grim!

155
00:20:45,670 --> 00:20:48,690
Thank you, Roald!

156
00:20:48,690 --> 00:20:51,180
Take care, everyone!

157
00:21:27,000 --> 00:21:27,960
Come here.

158
00:21:41,140 --> 00:21:42,940
Good boy.

159
00:21:43,860 --> 00:21:46,230
Carve it.

160
00:21:46,560 --> 00:21:47,820
Hup!

161
00:21:56,240 --> 00:22:01,120
Carve it into your flesh.
Carve it into the land.

162
00:22:07,380 --> 00:22:09,130
Carve it into the sea.

163
00:22:14,890 --> 00:22:19,520
Carve it into your spoils.
Carve it into your enemies.

164
00:22:20,690 --> 00:22:22,060
Carve it.

165
00:22:23,310 --> 00:22:25,070
Carve it.

166
00:22:25,070 --> 00:22:28,820
Boss, when are you going to
start working? Come on.

167
00:22:29,240 --> 00:22:33,290
Shut up. I was just taking a little break.

168
00:22:33,700 --> 00:22:36,990
I'll show you what farm
work really looks like.

169
00:22:36,990 --> 00:22:39,200
Oh, yeah? Let's see it, then.

170
00:22:40,250 --> 00:22:43,210
I'll get this done in a snap.

171
00:22:43,210 --> 00:22:46,460
Carve what you feel into me.

172
00:23:00,420 --> 00:23:07,180
In my life, I've always endured.

173
00:23:08,200 --> 00:23:13,260
I thought that pain was
the way of the world.

174
00:23:18,950 --> 00:23:23,650
I never thought I'd meet men like them.

175
00:23:23,650 --> 00:23:24,990
Right, Arnheid?

176
00:23:29,050 --> 00:23:38,050
They're headed toward a world
we never even imagined.

177
00:23:41,190 --> 00:23:45,870
Someplace that's not here.

178
00:23:49,230 --> 00:23:56,530
Carve that encounter into me.

179
00:25:36,170 --> 00:25:39,680
Home.

180
00:25:37,510 --> 00:25:38,830
"Home."
